tor tabs and Sections content (Contact Info, About Me, Academic Background, Career History, Core Competencies) remained intact. Clicked 'Show Preview' again - preview reappeared and Template tab still showed 'minimal' as selected, confirming no loss of editor content or template selection.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-6\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Duplicated 'QA Engineer Resume - Draft' via card menu -> Duplicate, creating 'QA Engineer Resume - Draft (Copy)' with identical content. Renamed the copy to 'Job Application - Company X' and changed its Full Name to 'Jane Copy Test'. Reopened the original resume: title remained 'QA Engineer Resume - Draft' and Full Name remained 'Jane Test', confirming the source was unaffected.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-7\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"During this session, created 'QA Engineer Resume - Draft' (new, Minimal template) and duplicated it into 'Job Application - Company X' (renamed, edited independently) alongside the 3 pre-existing seed resumes (Software Engineer, Marketing Manager, Product Designer). Dashboard lists all 5 distinct resumes simultaneously with independent titles/content/templates, demonstrating management of multiple variations for different applications.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-8\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Searched lowercase 'marketing' and it matched 'Marketing Manager Resume' (case-insensitive). Cleared search and all 5 resumes reappeared. Selected 'Oldest First' sort: order became Jan 2024 -> Feb 2024 -> Feb 2024 -> Aug 2026 -> Aug 2026 (ascending). Selected 'Newest First': order reverted to descending by date.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-19\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No date filter feature exists on the dashboard\", \"actual\": \"The dashboard only provides a title search textbox and a sort dropdown (Newest First/Oldest First/Title A-Z/Title Z-A). There is no exact-date or date-range filter control anywhere on the page (confirmed via full accessibility snapshot), so users cannot narrow saved resumes by creation date at all.\", \"evidence\": \"Full browser_snapshot of the dashboard shows only a search textbox and sort combobox; no date input, date-range picker, or date filter UI is present.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-9\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Invalid experience date periods (end before start, future dates) are silently accepted with no validation feedback\", \"actual\": \"Set End Date to 2019-01 while Start Date was 2020-01 (end precedes start): the value was saved with no error message, no aria-invalid attribute, and no visual error indication (checked full outerHTML of the entry, and re-observed the field which retained the invalid value). Also set Start Date to 2027-01 (a future date, today is 2026-08-25): also accepted silently with no rejection or feedback. Reverted values afterward to avoid corrupting other tests.\", \"evidence\": \"semantic_observe of editor.experience.item.pgn0tnmupb.end-date returned value '2019-01' after being set below the start date '2020-01', and start-date returned '2027-01' after being set in the future, both with no error UI in the surrounding DOM.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-10\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Experience and Education date fields both use HTML month-picker inputs (type='month', YYYY-MM format) and render consistently as 'Mon YYYY' in the preview (e.g. 'Jan 2020 - Jun 2023', 'Aug 2013 - May 2017'). Toggling 'I currently work here' on the QualityWorks experience entry cleared the End Date value to '' and disabled the field (enabled:false), and the preview showed 'Jan 2020 Present'. Unchecking it re-enabled the End Date field.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-11\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No data persistence across page reload - all session changes are lost\", \"actual\": \"Before reload, the dashboard had 4 resumes: 'Job Application - Company X' (duplicated+renamed+edited), 'QA Engineer Resume - Draft' (newly created+edited), 'Marketing Manager Resume', and 'Software Engineer Resume' (Product Designer Resume had just been deleted). After navigating to http://localhost:6005/ again (reload), the dashboard reverted to the original 3 seed resumes ('Product Designer Resume', 'Marketing Manager Resume', 'Software Engineer Resume') - the created resume and the duplicate both vanished entirely, and the deleted 'Product Designer Resume' reappeared. No created, edited, duplicated, renamed, or deleted changes survived the reload.\", \"evidence\": \"Dashboard collection before reload: [Job Application - Company X, QA Engineer Resume - Draft, Marketing Manager Resume, Software Engineer Resume]. Dashboard collection after reload: [Product Designer Resume, Marketing Manager Resume, Software Engineer Resume] - identical to the app's initial seed state.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-21\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Empty/whitespace title rejection has no validation feedback message\", \"actual\": \"Editing the title and submitting a whitespace-only value ('   ') was rejected in the sense that the title correctly reverted to 'QA Engineer Resume - Draft' (title was NOT changed to whitespace), but no validation feedback of any kind was shown - the Notifications region remained empty and no error text appeared anywhere in the page body. The checklist requires the user to receive clear validation feedback, which is absent.\", \"evidence\": \"After submitting whitespace title, browser_snapshot showed Notifications (F8) region with an empty list, and a full-page text search for 'required'/'cannot be empty'/'Title' found none of these strings present.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-12\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Throughout contact/summary/experience/education/skills edits, the preview.document region updated immediately after each keystroke/add/remove/reorder action with no manual save or refresh performed (e.g., typing 'Jane Test' instantly appeared in preview.contact.name; added experience/education/skills entries appeared instantly in preview lists).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Section reorder and visibility toggle changes reflected in the preview immediately with no manual save/refresh. Will further verify persistence across dashboard navigation as part of CT-16/IX-14 checks.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-14\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Edits made across multiple editor tabs were retained after clicking Back to dashboard and reopening the resume (all fields intact as observed). Dashboard card showed 'Updated Aug 25, 2026' (today's date), reflecting the update.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-15\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Added 4 experience entries plus existing education/skills to force content beyond the visible viewport (body scrollHeight 2018px vs window height 720px). All visible sections (Contact/banner, Summary, Education, 4 Experience entries, Skills) with content rendered fully and completely in the DOM (verified via browser_snapshot), and the page became scrollable so the full resume remains reachable/readable via scroll rather than being clipped.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-16\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"After navigating through Contact/Summary/Experience/Education/Skills/Template/Sections tabs, returning to dashboard, and reopening the resume, all contact fields (Jane Test, jane.test@email.com, etc.), summary text, experience entry (QualityWorks Inc./QA Automation Lead), education entry (University of Texas), and skill (Selenium) were all present and unchanged.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-17\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Editing the duplicate's Full Name field to 'Jane Copy Test' did not alter the original resume's Full Name, which remained 'Jane Test' upon reopening.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-18\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Renamed resume title to 'QA Engineer Resume - Draft'. Dashboard card immediately showed this title. Reopening the resume from the dashboard showed the same title in the editor.title field.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-20\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Customized section heading not rendered for Contact section in any style; Summary heading not rendered in Minimal style\", \"actual\": \"Renamed 'Contact Information' heading to 'Contact Info' in the Sections tab, but the preview never renders any heading for the contact section in Modern, Classic, or Minimal styles (only the person's name appears, no section title). Also renamed Summary heading to 'About Me': it appears correctly in Modern and Classic previews, but is completely omitted in the Minimal preview even though the summary text itself is visible there. Experience, Education, and Skills customized headings (Career History, Academic Background, Core Competencies) rendered correctly in all three styles.\", \"evidence\": \"browser_snapshot of preview.document across modern/classic/minimal templates shows no 'Contact Info' heading text anywhere, and Minimal preview's summary block is a bare paragraph with no preceding heading, while Modern/Classic show heading 'About Me'.\"}]}"
      }
    ]
  }
